</span>
Create a custom OAuth 2.0 / OIDC provider (Atlas is the relying party). OIDC: give the issuer and the endpoints are discovered (a bad issuer is a 400 now, not a broken button later). OAuth 2.0: give the authorize, token and userinfo endpoints. Set client authentication (client_secret_basic/post/jwt,<span pulumi-lang-nodejs=" privateKeyJwt " pulumi-lang-dotnet=" PrivateKeyJwt " pulumi-lang-go=" privateKeyJwt " pulumi-lang-python=" private_key_jwt " pulumi-lang-yaml=" privateKeyJwt " pulumi-lang-java=" privateKeyJwt " pulumi-lang-hcl=" private_key_jwt "> privateKeyJwt </span>with an Atlas-held key, or none), a declarative profile_mapping, upstream logout and third-party initiated login. The response names the URLs to register at the provider. Starts disabled unless `enabled: true` (which needs a client id, a secret for the secret methods, and a signing key for private_key_jwt).

Scopes: `oauth_providers:read` to read, `oauth_providers:write` to write.

Backend API: `POST /v1/custom_oauth_providers` (create); `GET /v1/custom_oauth_providers/{id}` (read); `PATCH /v1/custom_oauth_providers/{id}` (update); `DELETE /v1/custom_oauth_providers/{id}` (destroy).

