## <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`perCallAudience`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`PerCallAudience`" pulumi-lang-go="`perCallAudience`" pulumi-lang-python="`per_call_audience`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`perCallAudience`" pulumi-lang-java="`perCallAudience`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`per_call_audience`">`perCallAudience`</span> block

Lets a token mint name its own audience per call (`getToken({ for, cbid })`, `?audience=`, or `?<param>=`), so one integration can serve many values (for example one audience per site). A preset already allows its own parameter for the configured value only (chatly <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`channel`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`Channel`" pulumi-lang-go="`channel`" pulumi-lang-python="`channel`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`channel`" pulumi-lang-java="`channel`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`channel`">`channel`</span>, forumulate and referalli <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`orgId`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`OrgId`" pulumi-lang-go="`orgId`" pulumi-lang-python="`org_id`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`orgId`" pulumi-lang-java="`orgId`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`org_id`">`orgId`</span>, cookiemunch <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`cbid`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`Cbid`" pulumi-lang-go="`cbid`" pulumi-lang-python="`cbid`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`cbid`" pulumi-lang-java="`cbid`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`cbid`">`cbid`</span>); set the block to allow more values. Omit it to keep the preset's default; set <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`perCallAudienceDisabled " pulumi-lang-dotnet="`PerCallAudienceDisabled " pulumi-lang-go="`perCallAudienceDisabled " pulumi-lang-python="`per_call_audience_disabled " pulumi-lang-yaml="`perCallAudienceDisabled " pulumi-lang-java="`perCallAudienceDisabled " pulumi-lang-hcl="`per_call_audience_disabled ">`perCallAudienceDisabled </span>= true` to turn it off (cannot be combined with the block).

