"> atlas.LogoutNotifyEndpoint
</span>
Register a logout fan-out endpoint. It is POSTed `logout_token=<jwt>` (application/x-www-form-urlencoded; OIDC Back-Channel Logout: iss, sub, sid, events, signed with the instance JWKS) whenever an Atlas session ends, plus one with sub and no sid when the user is banned, deleted or deprovisioned. With<span pulumi-lang-nodejs=" oauthClientId " pulumi-lang-dotnet=" OauthClientId " pulumi-lang-go=" oauthClientId " pulumi-lang-python=" oauth_client_id " pulumi-lang-yaml=" oauthClientId " pulumi-lang-java=" oauthClientId " pulumi-lang-hcl=" oauth_client_id "> oauthClientId </span>it follows one OAuth client instead (that client's sign-in ending, incl. /oauth2/session/end and grant revocation). Retried on network errors, 5xx, 408 and 429; redirects are not followed. The URL must be public https.

Scopes: `logout_notify_endpoints:read` to read, `logout_notify_endpoints:write` to write.

Backend API: `POST /v1/logout_notify_endpoints` (create); `GET /v1/logout_notify_endpoints/{id}` (read); `PATCH /v1/logout_notify_endpoints/{id}` (update); `DELETE /v1/logout_notify_endpoints/{id}` (destroy).

## Example Usage

