category; the <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`label`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`Label`" pulumi-lang-go="`label`" pulumi-lang-python="`label`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`label`" pulumi-lang-java="`label`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`label`">`label`</span> is shown on the end-user's notification-preference toggle.
A tenant category is always optional — it cannot shadow a built-in category
(<span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`newDevice`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`NewDevice`" pulumi-lang-go="`newDevice`" pulumi-lang-python="`new_device`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`newDevice`" pulumi-lang-java="`newDevice`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`new_device`">`newDevice`</span>, <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`unattendedAccess`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`UnattendedAccess`" pulumi-lang-go="`unattendedAccess`" pulumi-lang-python="`unattended_access`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`unattendedAccess`" pulumi-lang-java="`unattendedAccess`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`unattended_access`">`unattendedAccess`</span>, <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`credentialChange`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`CredentialChange`" pulumi-lang-go="`credentialChange`" pulumi-lang-python="`credential_change`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`credentialChange`" pulumi-lang-java="`credentialChange`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`credential_change`">`credentialChange`</span>) — and is what a
