"> atlas.PartnerPlatform
</span>
This instance as a **partner platform** of another product: a product that signs the events it delivers to you (for example consent events) with a published Ed25519 key set. Atlas verifies each delivery against the partner's key set and applies it to your users. One resource per partner. A preset partner fills in the defaults on create. The partner token is **write-only** (<span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`tokenWo`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`TokenWo`" pulumi-lang-go="`tokenWo`" pulumi-lang-python="`token_wo`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`tokenWo`" pulumi-lang-java="`tokenWo`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`token_wo`">`tokenWo`</span>): it is stored once, encrypted, and never returned or kept in state. <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`tokenWo`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`TokenWo`" pulumi-lang-go="`tokenWo`" pulumi-lang-python="`token_wo`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`tokenWo`" pulumi-lang-java="`tokenWo`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`token_wo`">`tokenWo`</span> needs Terraform 1.11 or later.

Attributes, defaults and replace-on-change rules are in the schema (`terraform providers schema -json`).

## Example Usage

