" pulumi-lang-python=" Policy
" pulumi-lang-yaml=" atlas.Policy
" pulumi-lang-java=" atlas.Policy
" pulumi-lang-hcl=" atlas_policy
"> atlas.Policy
</span>
A policy your users accept: terms of service, a privacy policy, any key. The
policy asks nobody anything until a version is published.

**Versions are content, so they are not managed by this resource.** Publish them
from the dashboard, the Backend API or SDKs (`policies.versions`), or serve them
from an external system with <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`atlas.PolicySource`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`atlas.PolicySource`" pulumi-lang-go="`PolicySource`" pulumi-lang-python="`PolicySource`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`atlas.PolicySource`" pulumi-lang-java="`atlas.PolicySource`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`atlas_policy_source`">`atlas.PolicySource`</span>.

Destroying the resource deletes a policy that was never published and *retires*
one with a published version (its acceptances are kept as evidence). A retired
policy is treated as gone: the next plan re-creates it, and applying revives the
retired policy that has the same <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`key`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`Key`" pulumi-lang-go="`key`" pulumi-lang-python="`key`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`key`" pulumi-lang-java="`key`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`key`">`key`</span>.

API: `POST /v1/policies`, `GET`/`PATCH`/`DELETE /v1/policies/{id}`.

