- <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`partnerLinkId`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`PartnerLinkId`" pulumi-lang-go="`partnerLinkId`" pulumi-lang-python="`partner_link_id`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`partnerLinkId`" pulumi-lang-java="`partnerLinkId`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`partner_link_id`">`partnerLinkId`</span>: the id of the partner link the orchestrator's owner granted this instance. Setting it makes Atlas call the orchestrator with that grant and turns on <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`usePartnerLink`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`UsePartnerLink`" pulumi-lang-go="`usePartnerLink`" pulumi-lang-python="`use_partner_link`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`usePartnerLink`" pulumi-lang-java="`usePartnerLink`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`use_partner_link`">`usePartnerLink`</span>. Removing it clears it.
- <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`cancelDeletionOnSignIn`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`CancelDeletionOnSignIn`" pulumi-lang-go="`cancelDeletionOnSignIn`" pulumi-lang-python="`cancel_deletion_on_sign_in`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`cancelDeletionOnSignIn`" pulumi-lang-java="`cancelDeletionOnSignIn`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`cancel_deletion_on_sign_in`">`cancelDeletionOnSignIn`</span>: cancel a pending account deletion when the person signs in again (the instance setting `compliance.retention.cancelDeletionOnSignIn`). Unset keeps the current setting.

